/* Pass-4 mechanism calibration (class-3 deferred campaign, Task 1).
   15 entries: f1, f2, f5 (the spec section 2.2 generic-parameter
   shapes) + 3.1.5 e186-e197 (the 12 F_-domain corpus texts, verbatim).
   Per entry: production trace (rubi_verbose), top-level op, factor
   census, the sweep with P4SCAN markers (the "rubi: rule ... fired
   on" line following a P4SCAN marker is that scan's top-level fire -
   the first such line after the marker; nested fires come later,
   during the repl), the diagnostic on products, and the verdict
   label. Commit the output as
   probes/corpus/06-class3-deferred-mechanisms.calibrate.out.

   Run under the rules core image (the package + the 3513-rule table
   are baked in; a fresh "maxima -b" has no table):
     sbcl --tls-limit 100000 --core test/mr_rules.core \
       --noinform --very-quiet -b probes/corpus/06-calibration.pass4.mac

   Build-note deviations from the brief's literal text (each measured
   2026-08-30, Maxima branch_5_50_base_84_g4204fb669 / SBCL 2.6.7):
   - string building uses concat(...) - in this build "+" on strings
     does NOT concatenate (it treats the string contents as symbols
     and returns their sum);
   - P4DIAG renders the diagnostic list via string(...) - the brief's
     sapply(lambda[[s],s], ...) errors on a flat list of strings;
   - rubi_verbose stays on THROUGH the sweep (the brief turns it off
     before the sweep, but Step 9 wants the sweep's "fired on" rule
     names recorded - the first such line after each P4SCAN marker);
    - the brief's "16 entries" is a typo: 3 f-forms + 12 F_-domain
      forms = 15.

    Mechanism fix this calibration pins (maxima_rubi_implicit1.lisp):
    the brief's Step-2 e-itself branch gated the leftover single-factor
    wrap on (null *mr-implicit1-which*), i.e. which=nil only. Measured
    2026-08-30: that guard 0-fired the which=i sweep (3_5_r43 on 3.1.5
    e186) because an inner-match single-factor findfun call bailed; the
    fix drops the guard (wrap for any which). Pass 3 (which=nil) is
    byte-identical - it wrapped before too. The m=1 rows (e186-e193)
    are the regression check for that fix: they 0-fired the sweep with
    the guard, fire 3_5_r43 without it. */
cali_entry(name, f, x) := block([ans, census, k, hp, d, i, ans4],
  print(concat("CALI ", name)),
  rubi_verbose : true,
  ans : rubi(f, x),
  print(concat("PROD ", if atom(ans) then "atom" else string(op(ans)))),
  census : %mr_barefactors(f),
  k : part(census, 1),
  hp : part(census, 2),
  print(concat("P4CENSUS ", string(k), " ", string(hp))),
  if is(op(f) = "*") then
    print(concat("P4DIAG ", string(%mr_p4_diag(f)))),
  if is(hp = false) and is(k >= 2) then (
    for d : 0 thru 1 do
      for i : 1 thru k do (
        print(concat("P4SCAN ", string(d), " ", string(i))),
        ans4 : %mr_p4_once(f, x, mr_rule_table, 1, d, i),
        if is(ans4 # false) then
          print(concat("P4FIRE ", string(d), " ", string(i), " ",
                       if atom(ans4) then "atom" else string(op(ans4))))
      )
  ) else print(concat("P4SKIP")),
  rubi_verbose : false,
  print(concat("CALIEND ", name)))$

/* f2 - production pass 3 fires a 3_1_5 rule and answers (spec 2.2). */
cali_entry("f2", (d+e*x)*(a+b*log(c*x^n)), x)$
/* f1 - 0-fires all three passes; explicit x^3 shadows the sweep. */
cali_entry("f1", x^3*(d+e*x)*(a+b*log(c*x^n)), x)$
/* f5 - mquot top, 0-fires. */
cali_entry("f5", (d+e*x)*(a+b*log(c*x^n))/x, x)$
/* 3.1.5 e186-e197, verbatim corpus texts, one cali_entry each. */
cali_entry("e186", (d+e*x^2)*asin(a*x)*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e187", (d+e*x^2)*acos(a*x)*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e188", (d+e*x^2)*atan(a*x)*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e189", (d+e*x^2)*acot(a*x)*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e190", (d+e*x^2)*asinh(a*x)*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e191", (d+e*x^2)*acosh(a*x)*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e192", (d+e*x^2)*atanh(a*x)*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e193", (d+e*x^2)*acoth(a*x)*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e194", (d+e*x^2)*asin(a*x)^2*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e195", (d+e*x^2)*acos(a*x)^2*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e196", (d+e*x^2)*asinh(a*x)^2*log(c*x^n), x)$
cali_entry("e197", (d+e*x^2)*acosh(a*x)^2*log(c*x^n), x)$
print(concat("CALIDONE"))$
